Useful candidate mappings to test exhaustively:

- foreground in A only;
- foreground in B only;
- foreground in either panel (union);
- foreground in both (intersection);
- foreground in exactly one (XOR);
- equal states / unequal states;
- literal overlay with a defined precedence.

Do not declare a candidate supported because it explains the highlighted cells; check every output cell including all background cells. If an output is smaller or one panel's geometry is different, map coordinates using the separator and demonstrated dimensions before trying Boolean rules. Preserve demo inputs/outputs as exact fixtures and assert complete equality after every code edit.
